# Open Brain — Ingest sidecar cron entries (Unraid host)
#
# INSTALL (post-merge, once):
#   1. SSH to homeserver as `claude` (has passwordless sudo for cron operations).
#   2. Append these lines to the Unraid system crontab:
#        sudo tee -a /boot/config/plugins/dynamix/custom.cron < deploy/cron/unraid-ingest.cron
#      Unraid reads /boot/config/plugins/dynamix/*.cron on boot and merges them
#      into the live crontab (same persistence path as the existing
#      scripts/backup.sh entry).
#   3. Reload cron so the lines take effect without a reboot:
#        sudo /usr/local/sbin/update_cron
#   4. Verify:
#        crontab -l | grep ingest
#
# ROLLBACK:
#   Remove the three lines from /boot/config/plugins/dynamix/custom.cron and
#   run update_cron again.
#
# LOGS:
#   /var/log/financial-ingest.log and /var/log/utility-ingest*.log rotate
#   via Unraid's default logrotate. Truncate manually with
#   `sudo : > /var/log/financial-ingest.log` if they grow large.
#
# CONSTRAINTS:
#   - Each command shells into a long-lived sidecar container via `docker exec`.
#     The container is `sleep infinity` today; CS3 replaces the CMD with
#     trigger_server.py, but the `docker exec python /app/<script>.py ...`
#     invocation keeps working either way (bypasses the main CMD).
#   - Lock contention is the sidecar script's responsibility. financial-pipeline
#     uses filesystem-based processed-dir moves which are naturally serialized
#     by the one-cron-at-a-time schedule.

# Financial inbox — scan daily at 6:00 AM local, parse anything dropped in
# /mnt/user/appdata/open-brain/financial-inbox/, post captures, move to
# processed/.
0 6 * * * /usr/bin/docker exec open-brain-financial-ingest python /app/financial-pipeline.py --process-inbox >> /var/log/financial-ingest.log 2>&1

# Utility gas + power — daily at 6:30 AM. Gas South billing fetch + Cobb EMC
# power-summary (reads CSVs produced by electric-usage-downloader — that tool
# is itself scheduled separately via the sidecar's own cron entry if/when
# it's wired; for now --power-summary is a no-op if no CSVs present).
30 6 * * * /usr/bin/docker exec open-brain-utility-ingest python /app/utility-pipeline.py --gas --power-summary >> /var/log/utility-ingest.log 2>&1

# Utility monthly comparison — 2nd of each month at 2 AM. Aggregates the
# prior month's water/gas/power data and posts a single synthesized capture.
# (Water is a no-op today — Cobb Water B2C OIDC is a separate backlog.)
0 2 2 * * /usr/bin/docker exec open-brain-utility-ingest python /app/utility-pipeline.py --monthly-comparison >> /var/log/utility-monthly.log 2>&1

# Financial daily balance snapshot + account monitoring — 7:00 AM and 7:05 AM daily.
# Run in sequence: --balances first (writes daily_balances rows), then --account-monitoring
# (reads those rows). Separate cron entries ensure correct ordering via the 5-minute gap.
# These are host-level cron jobs — no collision with BullMQ scheduler slots (0 7 budget-check
# runs inside the workers container; these exec into open-brain-financial-ingest).
0 7 * * * /usr/bin/docker exec open-brain-financial-ingest python /app/financial-pipeline.py --balances >> /var/log/financial-balances.log 2>&1
5 7 * * * /usr/bin/docker exec open-brain-financial-ingest python /app/financial-pipeline.py --account-monitoring >> /var/log/financial-monitoring.log 2>&1

# Actual Budget daily job (#311) — 6:00 AM local (America/New_York). runBankSync,
# T0-categorize new uncategorized transactions, Pushover summary, one aggregated
# capture. Node sidecar (not python). Same minute as financial-ingest is fine —
# different container, and financial-ingest is idle post-D138. OA-18.
0 6 * * * /usr/bin/docker exec open-brain-actual-ingest node /app/actual-daily.mjs >> /var/log/actual-ingest.log 2>&1
